;SPLICE2: READ ANOTHER 2D INPUT UFILE ? (Y/N; "Q" EXITS):$
*T ==> the "splice2" utility patches together 2d Ufiles on a common axis
*T ==> the user chooses the axis of splicing; the other coordinate axis
*T ==> must be identical for all input files.
;SPLICE2: READ ANOTHER 2D INPUT UFILE ? (Y/N; "Q" EXITS):$
Y
;UFNTER:  ENTER OPCODE (D/E/F/P/S/Q... ):$
F A EC1 Q
;SPLICE2:  ENTER 5 DIGIT SHOT #, "Q" TO BACK UP$
37065
;SPLICE2:  SPECIFY FIXED COORDINATE "1" OR "2":$
2
;SPLICE2: READ ANOTHER 2D INPUT UFILE ? (Y/N; "Q" EXITS):$
Y
;UFNTER:  ENTER OPCODE (D/E/F/P/S/Q... ):$
F A EC2 Q
;SPLICE2:  ENTER 5 DIGIT SHOT #, "Q" TO BACK UP$
37065
;SPLICE2:  USE INPUT DATA?  (Y/N):$
Y
;SPLICE2: READ ANOTHER 2D INPUT UFILE ? (Y/N; "Q" EXITS):$
N
;SPLICE2:  ENTER OPCODE:$
B
;INORD:  ENTER NEW ITEM OR OPTION FOR LIST "SPLICE2":$
0 3 5 7
;INORD:  ENTER NEW ITEM OR OPTION FOR LIST "SPLICE2":$
Q
;SPLICE2: ENTER INTERVAL # TO MODIFY DATA ASSOCIATION, OR "Q":$
1 0
;SPLICE2: ENTER INTERVAL # TO MODIFY DATA ASSOCIATION, OR "Q":$
3 0
;SPLICE2: ENTER INTERVAL # TO MODIFY DATA ASSOCIATION, OR "Q":$
5 0
;SPLICE2: ENTER INTERVAL # TO MODIFY DATA ASSOCIATION, OR "Q":$
4 2
;SPLICE2: ENTER INTERVAL # TO MODIFY DATA ASSOCIATION, OR "Q":$
Q
;SPLICE2:  ENTER OPCODE:$
G
;SPLICE2:  SPECIFY FILE #, "L" TO LIST, "Q" TO QUIT:$
L
;SPLICE2:  SPECIFY FILE #, "L" TO LIST, "Q" TO QUIT:$
1 1 P
